("v386", "scalar", "✔ every embedded activity keeps its artwork visible independently of reader breakpoints (6.5591ms)\n✔ every encounter has a crawler-readable canonical page and complete sharing metadata (40.386ms)\n✔ the social image is a real correctly described bitmap; sitemap includes all canonical pages (6.895ms)\n✔ all local links and assets in the new static pages resolve within the publication (519.8337ms)\n✔ historical oracle bytes, passive resources and declared mechanism successors remain pinned (161.518ms)\n✔ algebra owns the publication with the existing admission rules, ports and budget (40.5148ms)\n✔ reading paths connect the guided journey to research while microsites keep their own entrances (35.1047ms)\n✔ the homepage presents the hierarchy and preserves existing project entrances (1.9017ms)\n✔ Claimipedia has its own three-lens identity with accessible sections, local assets and quiet motion (8.8131ms)\n✔ purpose-first sharing cards have real raster bytes and consistent server-visible metadata (27.7555ms)\n✔ a fresh algebra build reproduces every publication artifact (69833.8981ms)\n✔ algebra remembers actual destination visits, deduplicates them and restores the map (27.2581ms)\n✔ reset clears only the atlas key and all seen labels (8.6563ms)\n✔ untrusted saved text is bounded and restricted to known places (12.4711ms)\n✔ blocked storage stays nonfatal and reports the limit honestly (10.0065ms)\n✔ previews are dismissible and every pin has an ordinary link and readable label (6.9514ms)\n✔ mobile taps preview a place before exploration, with no false seen mark (6.3193ms)\n✔ a destination restored from browser history marks itself again after a reset (1.7109ms)\n✔ the independent illustrated atlas preserves all forty destinations and return paths (28.3458ms)\n✔ source ownership switches only after ordered module and lowering correspondence, then validation (10.3347ms)\n✔ stale, ambiguous, undeclared and non-corresponding migrations cannot stage (20.7321ms)\n✔ all six retained predecessors pass the actual authoring algebra, shared frontend and whole-module lowerer (13551.0881ms)\n✔ acceptance matches command identity, count, exit status and error rather than PASS strings or ok flags (12.1636ms)\n✔ retirement preserves exact helper bytes before deletion and ignores logs/directories (1.138ms)\n✔ archive collisions refuse retirement and source switching before validation (2.2704ms)\n✔ clean verification requires a clean revision and absent build, installed dependencies and generated output (1.0067ms)\n✔ normal verification has no .build input and does not rewrite presentation evidence (228.2467ms)\n✔ snapshot comparison hashes binary input bytes and distinguishes an absent creation target (7.1895ms)\n✔ retired helpers remain hashed evidence with no active executable counterpart (6.1782ms)\n✔ the authoring policy admits with only its declared generic mechanisms (218.7503ms)\n✔ previews validate without committing; apply commits the validated proposal before its receipt (2.2653ms)\n✔ bad authority, stale and repeated edits, no-ops and malformed proposals refuse before staging (3.4667ms)\n✔ failed publication validation cannot reach the commit effect (0.6006ms)\n✔ all build source owners remain editable; generator predecessors are inert and byte-identical (6.8057ms)\n✔ encounter: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (12012.1706ms)\n✔ source: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (204.9414ms)\n✔ microsite-ui: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (223.081ms)\n✔ microsite-values: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (209.0415ms)\n✔ microsite-sourcery: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (158.7376ms)\n✔ microsite-temple-ui: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (698.9401ms)\n✔ all six explicit effect profiles link against the same supplied application closure (52.731ms)\n✔ each is profile-gated and preserves binding, ordered effects and non-accumulating scope (808.2159ms)\n✔ module-specific profiles refuse foreign source profiles, effects and undeclared callees (1290.0918ms)\n✔ JSON and candidate UI legs preserve ordered DOM/state effects, recipe values and crypto refusal (1104.1467ms)\n✔ the pre-switch JSON owner or post-switch Encounter owner is explicit, never a fallback (5536.6331ms)\n✔ all 48 bounded reviews correspond to the original Claimipedia evaluator (57.1384ms)\n✔ reasoning exposes failed conditions, omitted evidence and the equal-weight blind spot (8.4655ms)\n✔ real Worldwright Markdown projects headings, two tables, strong text and honest source-relative links (94.9289ms)\n✔ Markdown projection preserves fenced blank lines, lists, quotes and literal unsafe markup (45.5109ms)\n✔ shared Markdown lexer preserves every source code unit and gives syntax real roles (101.07ms)\n✔ readable expression layout breaks long groups without modifying its input model (3.4578ms)\n✔ Markdown projection refuses documents outside its declared bounds (28.4995ms)\n✔ every source query has a readable definition and exact structural statement coordinates (372.7355ms)\n✔ readable module inspection refuses missing queries and does not execute source effects (1.6931ms)\n✔ the module selector projects the bound query through the shared presenter using read-only DOM effects (802.3921ms)\n✔ the standalone module page replaces the raw-JSON entrance and states the authoring boundary (2.0313ms)\n✔ microsite and every declared event root admit against the existing kernel and grants (1196.6264ms)\n✔ the live title edit uses the original patch contract and updates exactly its source-derived views (1041.143ms)\n✔ wrong value types and fields without a declared inverse route refuse (462.2295ms)\n✔ every inspector selection exposes the current exact text and a shared highlighted projection (1633.8331ms)\n✔ boot, edit, inspection and reset share one session and preserve the accepted candidate on refusal (2514.7541ms)\n✔ the source owners reuse the retained compiler and leave the original microsites intact (6.1256ms)\n✔ each of the ten identified areas has a distinct, sourced and rendered entrance and continuation (4.5684ms)\n✔ every selected corpus source preserves its retained capture and recorded hash (15.1747ms)\n✔ optional readings have explicit scope and do not gate a scientific route (0.6512ms)\n✔ the finite compatibility example exposes its exact allowed set (0.4299ms)\n✔ the pattern counter applies the declared integer action without treating ornament as evidence (0.359ms)\n✔ positive-response admission agrees with the smallest eigenvalue on every displayed matrix (3.0666ms)\n✔ the repetition-code claim holds over both original bits and all eight received words (0.4134ms)\n✔ the numerical memory illustration remains finite and changes when coupling is removed (0.3641ms)\n✔ block aggregation preserves total while discarding within-block arrangements (0.4078ms)\n✔ the ranking desk discloses a reversible arithmetic preference rather than changing the options (0.439ms)\n✔ reported rate cards retain the source decimals and their model-local intermediate optimum (0.6587ms)\n✔ encounters and paths beyond a territory preserve real destinations and source identity (1.714ms)\n✔ the illustrative measuring axis resolves a vertical unit difference only as it rotates toward it (0.3488ms)\n✔ lifting the map preserves the record while exposing conditions and limits separately (1.2881ms)\n✔ territories locate each scene exactly once and reflective studies retain their declared material (2.5819ms)\n✔ all passages resolve, all scenes are reachable, and every scene has a route back (2.0582ms)\n✔ each scene retains source identity and every cited corpus capture exists locally (8.7307ms)\n✔ personal passages are marked as personal and cannot be mistaken for model results (0.5768ms)\n✔ the homepage hierarchy preserves the author order and routes every tool to its own microsite (7.9634ms)\n✔ source snapshots preserve their hashes and exact upstream lines when the recorded source is available (73.8299ms)\n✔ all published capability edges are extracted by the existing REL parser with exact source bindings (137.7814ms)\n✔ sharing uses exact typed identity and counts each consumer once (7.3205ms)\n✔ malformed, unsupported and stale source-line bindings refuse rather than fabricating connections (4.6992ms)\n✔ source inspection exposes receipts, consumers and honest missing edges with the existing source presenter (3.7368ms)\n✔ the admitted viewer highlights source and its actual sharing definition with separate exact hash bases (1745.0737ms)\n✔ the opening fold has three illustrated entrances and moves questions and applications to their own destinations (1.591ms)\n✔ Mission Control is a first-class Sourcery tool, linked from Science, with inspected sources and native workflow disclosure (1.0565ms)\n✔ purpose types distinguish all cards while Creator Studio completes six developing entries (7.1684ms)\n✔ SHA-256 fallback agrees with Web Crypto for Unicode and padding boundaries (18.4416ms)\n✔ Temple Merkle drawing geometry, order, labels and fresh highlights match original SVG effects (235.2651ms)\n✔ Temple explanatory lessons match every preset, identity and refusal branch in the source (291.5584ms)\n✔ Sourcery flood scatter, waves and broom poses match original motion at sampled frames (102.0908ms)\n✔ Temple sky scatter, twinkle, parallax, motes and respawn match original canvas effects (128.7145ms)\n✔ Temple constellation geometry, glow, sparks and rings match original canvas effects (46.4578ms)\n✔ reduced motion and hidden documents draw still frames without scheduling animation (7.7059ms)\n✔ film seeking preserves range endpoints and the metadata/blob fallback sequence (2.6503ms)\n✔ Temple genesis identities, canonical bytes, state roots and Merkle levels match the original (36.6406ms)\n✔ every preset, identity and false-root choice reproduces the original proposal, verdict and witness (2187.9153ms)\n✔ amendment, refusals, stale basis, replay and both forgeries preserve the exact history boundary (732.3316ms)\n✔ Sourcery intent classification and all proposal templates match the original source (675.2785ms)\n✔ Sourcery sealing, returns, witness verification, tampering and restoration match the original (57.1177ms)\n✔ all four recomposed documents retain their independently compared source structure and reading (8.5743ms)\n✔ microsite navigation and referenced resources stay inside the ecosystem and resolve, including fragments (51.5638ms)\n✔ every captured microsite asset and both complete stylesheets retain their exact bytes (57.5165ms)\n✔ original application JavaScript is an oracle only; shipping behaviour is algebra-owned (15.6122ms)\n✔ every project microsite has exactly one algebra-owned return to the main catalogue (7.7638ms)\n✔ whole-module source compiles to exact ordered JSON with no profile or implicit entrypoint (4029.275ms)\n✔ every actual statement has an original-coordinate source origin (14.6616ms)\n✔ the entire lowered module is identical through the existing lowerer (1009.7259ms)\n✔ JSON and readable-source legs agree on real documents, formatting, faults and ordered effects (2333.51ms)\n✔ the successor changes only the declared lexer separator and safe record-key formatting (3.1014ms)\n✔ malformed control syntax, unsafe names, unknown operators and mismatched profile refuse (87.9171ms)\n✔ compiler identity refuses changed dependencies before compilation (2.9352ms)\n✔ linking traverses folds and error handlers and refuses undeclared calls or effects (30.7341ms)\n✔ a readable source edit changes execution through the existing lowerer and kernel (50.2464ms)\n✔ the authority switch selects Encounter exclusively and binds generated JSON to its source hash (3.2353ms)\n✔ Inspect displays exact authored characters using compiler ranges rather than regenerated notation (929.0638ms)\n✔ all bundled research sources preserve their recorded bytes (31.3271ms)\n✔ static entry points and module imports remain relative to their publication path (51.2419ms)\n✔ migrated finite models reproduce every slider setting and bit pattern (40.423ms)\n✔ both numerical memory trajectories and all plotted coordinates retain exact predecessor results (62.0994ms)\n✔ algebra-owned workshop sessions reproduce source edits, overlays, generated HTML and refusal boundaries (4430.9976ms)\n✔ forty activity source documents retain controls and contain no executable source (0.4904ms)\n✔ the published execution graph contains only admitted bundles and generic native mechanisms (127.5574ms)\n✔ whole-bundle auditing rejects extra executable code and altered native mechanisms (9.2142ms)\n✔ document observation executes supplied transformation plans without reader defaults (0.4836ms)\n✔ frame capability choice comes from algebra within the native script-free ceiling (2.5442ms)\n✔ every stop has an authored reading and every offered term has a definition (6.5007ms)\n✔ all sources have a plain introduction while original research and full source notes remain available (9.1828ms)\n✔ rate cards explain the same reported values as rounded percentages (0.8261ms)\n✔ the historical workshop oracle preserves its exact kernel and native function bodies (9.5364ms)\n✔ workshop is a connected tour stop with real static resources (1.0649ms)\n✔ all unaffected scenes retain the captured content of the other changes (1.6941ms)\n▶ portable engine preserves source/overlay ownership and unchanged-state refusals\n  ✔ starts from the checked fixture (0.2398ms)\n  ✔ source edit updates page and row, preserving overlay (0.2496ms)\n  ✔ overlay edits its literal and escapes generated markup (0.2834ms)\n  ✔ refuse /EC-T007/ (458.8582ms)\n  ✔ refuse /EC-E010/ (39.786